    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "status": "supported",
      "witness": null,
      "reason": "The claim lists three factors: (1) max repayment status (pay_max, a2: -0.5181, decreases_risk), (2) credit amount (LIMIT_BAL, a3: -0.4597, decreases_risk), and (3) amount paid (PAY_AMT1, a4: 0.4259, increases_risk). The text correctly identifies PAY_AMT1 as increasing risk, and the other two as contributing factors without misstating their directions. The phrase 'other contributing factors include' does not assert that all are risk-increasing; it merely lists them. The evidence supports all values and directions. The 'needs_assessment' reason ('one direction stated for several drivers with different signs') is misleading — the claim does not assign a single direction to all; it correctly attributes 'increases' only to PAY_AMT1."
